  "findings": [
    "The readout gap collapsed 1.6323 -> 0.3126 nats: 80.8% of it was a small-data artifact.",
    "Ten times the data helps the full readout 5.0x more than the low-rank one (-1.6505 vs -0.3308 nats), which is the signature of a head that was memorising rather than generalising.",
    "A residual advantage survives: 0.3126 nats and 1.67 accuracy points at matched compute.",
    "The 3,956,469-parameter model trained on 10,000 stories is the best of the four: CE 2.9493, 37.43% top-1, 1.039 nats below the released 52,756,661-parameter reference."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Neither 10k arm converged (1.83 passes). The residual 0.313-nat gap may be a convergence-rate difference rather than a final-quality difference; separating them requires training both to convergence on the larger corpus.",
    "Both 10k arms are budget-capped, so their trainer status is 'debug_stopped' with debug=true. That flags the cap, not a failure.",
    "Still no randomized-graph or zero-edge control, so nothing here speaks to whether the connectome itself contributes.",
    "The audit population was revealed by an earlier audit and is no longer untouched. The reserved 100-story test remains unopened."
  ],
